.TH TETROMINO 6 "2026-09-24" "tetromino 1.0.1" "Games"
.SH NAME
tetromino \- falling-block puzzle game for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tetromino
.RB [ \-\-size
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-difficulty
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-level
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-seed
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-color
.IR MODE ]
.RB [ \-\-mono ]
.RB [ \-\-fps
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-debug ]
.br
.B tetromino
.RB \-h | \-\-help | \-V | \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tetromino
is a falling-block puzzle game that runs in a terminal.
Seven kinds of four-square pieces fall into a well; move and rotate them to
fill complete rows, which then disappear.
The game ends when the stack reaches the top.
.PP
The start screen is a setup menu where you choose a board size and a
difficulty.
The board is drawn at the largest size that fits the terminal, and the
terminal is restored when the game exits, including on errors and signals.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-size " NAME"
Pre-select the board in the start menu:
.B small
(8\(mu16),
.B classic
(10\(mu20, default),
.B wide
(14\(mu20) or
.B tall
(10\(mu24).
.TP
.BI \-\-difficulty " NAME"
Pre-select the difficulty:
.BR easy ,
.B normal
(default),
.B hard
or
.BR expert .
See
.BR DIFFICULTY .
.TP
.BI \-\-level " N"
Start at level
.I N
(1\-30, default 1).
The difficulty may add further levels.
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " N"
Use a fixed random seed.
The same seed gives the same sequence of pieces on every machine.
.TP
.BI \-\-color " MODE"
Force the colour mode:
.BR truecolor ,
.BR 256 ,
.B 16
or
.BR mono .
By default it is detected from
.BR COLORTERM " and " TERM .
.TP
.B \-\-mono
Same as
.BR "\-\-color mono" .
.TP
.BI \-\-fps " N"
Maximum render rate, 10\-240 (default 60).
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Write a debug log (see
.BR FILES ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of options and controls.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH CONTROLS
.SS Start menu
.TP 16
.BR \(ua " " \(da " or " W " " S
Choose the board or difficulty row.
.TP
.BR \(<- " " \(-> " or " A " " D
Change the selected option.
.TP
.B Enter
Start the game.
.TP
.BR Q " or " Esc
Quit.
.SS Playing
.TP 16
.BR \(<- " " \(-> " or " A " " D
Move the piece.
.TP
.BR \(ua ", " W " or " X
Rotate clockwise.
.TP
.B Z
Rotate counter-clockwise.
.TP
.BR \(da " or " S
Soft drop (one row).
.TP
.B Space
Hard drop.
.TP
.B C
Hold the current piece (if the difficulty allows it).
.TP
.BR P " or " Esc
Pause and resume.
.TP
.B R
Restart (when paused or after game over).
.TP
.B M
Back to the setup menu (when paused or after game over).
.TP
.BR Q " or " Ctrl\-C
Quit.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-Z
Suspend to the shell; resume with
.BR fg .
.SH DIFFICULTY
.TS
l l l l l l.
Difficulty	Fall speed	Start level	Hold	Next pieces	Ghost
Easy	1.5\(mu slower	+0	yes	5	yes
Normal	standard	+0	yes	3	yes
Hard	0.6\(mu	+2	no	1	yes
Expert	0.35\(mu	+4	no	0	no
.TE
.PP
The level rises every 10 cleared lines.
Clearing 1, 2, 3 or 4 lines at once scores 100, 300, 500 or 800 points
multiplied by the level; soft drops score 1 point per row and hard drops
2 points per row.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set to a non-empty value, disables colour.
.TP
.BR COLORTERM ", " TERM
Used to detect colour support.
.TP
.B TETROMINO_DEBUG
If set to a value other than 0, enables debug logging, like
.BR \-\-debug .
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Base directory for the debug log (default
.IR ~/.local/state ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/tetromino/tetromino.log
Debug log, written only with
.B \-\-debug
or
.BR TETROMINO_DEBUG .
.SH NOTES
The terminal must use UTF-8 and be at least 50\(mu20 for the menu and about
58\(mu22 for the classic board (the menu shows the exact size needed).
Colour terminals get 24-bit colour, with fallbacks to 256 and 16 colours.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on normal exit, 1 on errors (for example when not run in a terminal),
2 for invalid command-line options.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at
.UR https://github.com/varuns2903/tetromino/issues
